  "report": "This patient has triple-negative breast cancer, which is associated with higher rates of pathologic complete response (pCR) to neoadjuvant therapy. However, the tumor is large with a volume of 34739 mm³ and is classified as high-risk by MammaPrint, both of which are negative prognostic factors for achieving pCR. The MRI shows a mass with heterogeneous enhancement and a central necrotic area. Given the conflicting factors—favorable subtype but unfavorable size and genomic risk—the estimated probability of pCR is moderate at approximately 55%, making the outcome uncertain."
}
